course: dictionary
lesson: 6035
title: Melt: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Melt can mean a change from solid to liquid, a slow fading away, or a soft feeling of kindness. Context tells you which one. «That is why an ice cube melts in your warm hand.» The warm hand is the clue: heat turns the solid ice into water, so melt means change into a liquid.
explain: «The crowd melted away.» Crowd and away are the clues. People do not turn into liquid, so melt here means slowly disappear. Check by swapping in your meaning: «The crowd slowly disappeared» still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: «Her heart melted when she saw the puppy.» Hearts do not turn to water. The clue is the feeling. Melt here means she became soft, loving and kind. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still works.
fact: Melt means to change from a solid into a liquid because of heat.
fact: «Chocolate melts just below body temperature», so it melts in your mouth but stays hard on a cool shelf.
fact: The temperature where a solid melts is its melting point: ice melts at 0 °C.
fact: Melting can be reversed by cooling, which is called freezing.
fact: «Melt away» means to slowly disappear, and «melt in your mouth» means to dissolve easily as you eat.
exercise: «That is why an ice cube melts in your warm hand.» What does melts mean here? | Goes very fast | Shines brightly | Becomes hard and cold | *Changes from a solid into a liquid because of heat
exercise: «The crowd melted away.» What does melted mean here? | Became a liquid | *Slowly disappeared | Stayed in one place | Grew bigger and louder
exercise: Nadia says melt is only about ice. What is the melting point of ice? | *0 °C | 430 °C | 100 °C | Minus 180 °C
test: «Her heart melted when she saw the puppy.» What does this suggest? | *She became kind and loving | She turned into water | She went cold and hard | She ran away from the puppy
test: Melting can be reversed by cooling. What is the word for cooling a liquid until it becomes solid again? | Shining | *Freezing | Melting | Boiling
exam: «Chocolate melts in your pocket and in your mouth but stays hard on a cool shelf.» Why does the chocolate stay hard on the shelf? | Chocolate never melts | The chocolate is too cool to melt | *The shelf is not warm enough to melt it | It is made of ice
